  "questions": [
    {
      "key": "d648ea05-9149-414f-ba2f-b3064911efd0",
      "id": "Q-01",
      "text": "At which distance bands does each of the four cameras detect, confirm and identify a Mavic 3 on the fly-area axis, and with what probability per bin?",
      "note": "Response: detection outcome per bin, per camera, per run (possible, confirmed, identified, none; FOV-limited flag). Vary: distance band (5 levels), camera configuration (4). Hold: altitude 40 m AGL, speed 5 m/s, aspect head-on, 30 s per band. Record: sun, sky background, wind, visibility. Replicates: 3 runs minimum (Appendix C.2). Target-absent interval: 120 s before launch, every run."
    }
