    "notes": "Run order: ladder first; it establishes the distance bins for the other profiles. Three replicate runs under the same conditions; add a fourth if two bins disagree between runs. Hover 30 s at 450, 350, 250, 150 and 75 m from the camera line, 40 m AGL, 5 m/s between bands, head-on aspect. Each hover gives every camera one 30 s observation interval per bin. Review each camera independently (plan section 7, step 6) and mark possible, confirmed and identified per bin; compute ground and slant range from the GCS log at each event. Before the first run: synchronize the PC, camera and telemetry clocks, record the offset with a visible time-marked event, and keep the correction (plan section 7, step 3). Safety: every path stays inside the UAS Fly Area; no path points at the camera site or at GCS-1. The One-way attack aim point sits 60 m short of the cameras. Site datum: the profile origin is the centre of the UAS Fly Area file (lat 35.289972, lon -79.385599, WGS84). Ground elevation 150 m is a planning value; survey it.",
